  faqs: [
    { question: "Where do I actually find an IB tutor in Nadiad?", answer: "Tell IB Gram your child's IB programme, subject, level and exam session, and a shortlist of tutors teaching exactly that course comes back. Since no school in Nadiad or Kheda district runs the Diploma, matching is based on syllabus fit nationally rather than location, with lesson timing confirmed to suit your household afterward. A free trial class always comes before anything else." },
    { question: "Can I get an IGCSE tutor in Nadiad for Cambridge subjects?", answer: "Yes. IGCSE tutors matched for Nadiad teach the Cambridge syllabus as online tuition rather than a home visit, matched to whatever specification a target school in Vadodara or Ahmedabad follows, or one your family is planning around. Matching runs by exact code and tier, commonly Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620, using genuine Cambridge past papers and mark schemes." },
    { question: "Will a tutor come to our house in Nadiad?", answer: "No. Nobody visits homes in Nadiad; that kind of in-person tuition is offered only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. Everywhere else, Nadiad included, a lesson happens live online, one to one, over video with a shared whiteboard. It is genuine tuition delivered at home, just without a tutor physically standing at your door." },
    { question: "How much should I expect to pay for a tutor in Nadiad?", answer: "The fee depends on the programme and level, the subject, session length and how recently the tutor taught that exact syllabus, and it gets confirmed for your specific case before the trial. IB Diploma HL subjects tend to cost more than Cambridge IGCSE Core support. Every session runs online, so no travel cost is hidden in the fee, and there is no long contract." },
    { question: "Does any school in Nadiad actually teach IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not that we could confirm. Every school we checked in Nadiad and the wider Kheda district runs the Gujarat state board or CBSE. The closest confirmed options sit in Vadodara, about an hour away, and Ahmedabad, roughly ninety minutes away." },
    { question: "My child boards at an IB school elsewhere. Can a Nadiad-based tutor help during the holidays?", answer: "Yes, and it is one of the more common requests we get from this part of Gujarat, precisely because no school in Nadiad teaches the IB Diploma or Middle Years Programme. A tutor gets matched to the exact subject, level and syllabus your child's boarding school follows, with sessions scheduled around school breaks or agreed evening slots where the school permits it." },
    { question: "Is there a trial class before we commit to anything?", answer: "Yes, every match starts with a free trial class. Your child works through a real topic from their own syllabus with the tutor online, at no cost and with no pressure to continue afterward. A short first-month plan follows, and the family decides whether to proceed, ask for changes, or try someone else entirely." },
    { question: "Will a tutor help write my child's IB Internal Assessment?", answer: "No, only guidance is on offer, never writing. That means helping choose a workable research question, explaining what an assessment criterion actually rewards, planning data collection, and giving honest feedback on drafts. Writing or rewriting assessed work breaks IB academic integrity rules outright, so IB Gram tutors will not do it." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can a Nadiad family actually get help with?", answer: "Tutors are matched across the major IB Diploma subject groups a boarding student connected to Nadiad is likely to need: Maths Analysis and Approaches or Applications and Interpretation at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, plus Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay." },
    { question: "Is MYP or PYP support available too, not just the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, the full IB continuum is covered for Nadiad households whose child attends an IB school elsewhere or is moving between curricula. MYP sessions focus on criterion-based analysis in sciences and language subjects, plus the Personal Project's process journal; PYP sessions build reading, number sense, writing and Exhibition research skills." },
    { question: "Is online tuition really as good as a tutor sitting in the room for a Nadiad student?", answer: "In practice, yes, particularly given Nadiad has no local IB or IGCSE school and effectively no local pool of specialists for either curriculum. A shared whiteboard, screen-shared past papers and recorded worked solutions cover almost everything an in-person tutor would otherwise offer, while opening up specialists from across India instead of a shortlist that does not exist locally." },
    { question: "How thoroughly does IB Gram vet its tutors for Nadiad students?", answer: "Every tutor is reviewed on qualifications, recent teaching experience at the exact subject and level, and their approach to assessment criteria before ever being introduced to a family. Given Nadiad has no local international-curriculum school, we specifically look for tutors with recent syllabus experience rather than generalists, and the free trial class lets a family judge the rest for themselves." },
    { question: "When is the best time for a Nadiad student to start tutoring?", answer: "Right at the course's start, Class 11 for the IB Diploma or Grade 9 for Cambridge IGCSE, since that leaves time to fix foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all land together. A student starting in the final year can still gain real ground, with sessions concentrated on the highest-value topics ahead of the exam series." },
    { question: "We are thinking about switching from the Gujarat board or CBSE to IGCSE. Can tutoring help?", answer: "Yes, and it is a common starting point for Nadiad families precisely because there is no local school's own choice to lean on. Sessions usually begin with a diagnostic look at where a child currently stands, then move to direct teaching of command words like explain, evaluate and justify, which decide IGCSE marks far more than raw content ever does." },
    { question: "Can sessions be arranged for weekends or evenings in Nadiad?", answer: "Yes, most families here book weekday evenings after school along with weekend mornings. Scheduling takes Kheda's summer heat into account, when earlier evening slots tend to be preferred, and Navratri and Uttarayan, when the local week shifts noticeably. Adding a second weekly slot before mocks or an exam series is easy to arrange." },
    { question: "What if a Nadiad family is not happy with the assigned tutor?", answer: "Say so, and a different tutor gets found. Progress is reviewed with families every few weeks specifically so a poor fit does not drag on unnoticed, and since there is no long contract, pausing or ending sessions never carries a penalty." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any tie-up with a Nadiad school, or with the IB or Cambridge itself?", answer: "No. IB Gram operates entirely independently, with no affiliation to, endorsement from or representation of any school named on this page, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Schools are named here purely to show where families connected to Nadiad actually study, and tutoring follows each school's own calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

